1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,190
Listen to a talk on a business podcast.

2
00:00:04,190 --> 00:00:05,996
M:

3
00:00:05,996 --> 00:00:12,095
When launching a new business, entrepreneurs face countless decisions, from choosing a target market

4
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:17,010
to deciding which features to include in their first product.

5
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:23,290
These choices can be overwhelming, especially when resources are limited and time is short.

6
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:33,030
To address these challenges, some startups adopt a strategy that emphasizes speed, experimentation, and customer feedback.

7
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:39,415
This approach, known as the Lean Startup methodology, was popularized by Eric Reese

8
00:00:39,415 --> 00:00:43,170
and has gained traction in the tech world and beyond.

9
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:51,110
One of its core practices is building a minimum viable product, or MVP.

10
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:55,368
This is a basic version of a new product that can be released quickly

11
00:00:55,368 --> 00:00:58,220
to gather feedback from early users.

12
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:01,930
The goal is to learn what works and what doesn't

13
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:09,130
so that future development is guided by actual user experience rather than assumptions.

14
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:13,090
Another key principle is validated learning.

15
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:21,036
Instead of doing traditional market research like surveys or focus groups, entrepreneurs test their

16
00:01:21,036 --> 00:01:25,110
ideas by putting the product out in the real world.

17
00:01:25,110 --> 00:01:32,010
This helps them figure out whether their product actually meets the needs of their customers.

18
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:37,220
In all fairness, I should point out that this approach isn't perfect.

19
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:42,929
Rapid iteration and constant feedback can sometimes lead to confusion

20
00:01:42,929 --> 00:01:45,120
or a lack of clear direction.

21
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:49,747
And in the pursuit of efficiency, some teams may cut corners,

22
00:01:49,747 --> 00:01:52,080
which could affect product quality.

23
00:01:52,080 --> 00:02:00,370
Still, many entrepreneurs find the Lean Startup methodology helpful for navigating the uncertainties of

24
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:03,080
launching a new business.
